Not bad, but get it on sale.
+ 2 very colourful characters (near the top tiers, generates feels);
+ Good voice acting and script;
+ Music was alright;
- Level design is a tunnel that connects point A to B;
- Combat is plain annoying;
Overall the game is worth to play through before you play Styx (it has this one thing that explains his origins). It feels as if ALL of the budget was spent to polish the 2 protagonists, starting from their textures down to the voice acting. Not much was left for anything else it seems. I am seriously sad that such a great duo of personalities were wasted on such a mediocre game design. Whatever RP elements there are such as levels and items - its all there just so that you could slap an RPG tag on it and min-max your stat, if you like that sort of thing. Personally I chose whichever has the dankest textures.
This "game" would have more value if it were a movie, seriously.
Play it on easy or something and pump your band of 2 with offensive abilities and have fun.

